{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>You shall rest.</b> Even from things that are not melakhah but are weekday exertion, as it says: וְכִבַּדְתּוֹ מֵעֲשׂוֹת דְּרָכֶיךָ, מִמְּצוֹא חֶפְצְךָ וְדַבֵּר דָּבָר (Isaiah 58:13)." "<b>That your ox and your donkey may rest.</b> When you rest even from such things as these." "<b>And the son of your maidservant and the stranger shall be refreshed.</b> From this it follows that the son of your maidservant and the stranger shall also be refreshed — the opposite of what happened to you in Egypt when you were a slave there and had no rest, as He said: תִּכְבַּד הָעֲבֹדָה עַל הָאֲנָשִׁים (Exodus 5:9). And through this you shall remember the exodus from Egypt, as He states in the commandments of Deuteronomy: וְזָכַרְתָּ כִּי עֶבֶד הָיִיתָ (Deuteronomy 5:14)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:56.779340630Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}